+<p><strong>Summary:</strong> ATERA provides full-transcriptome
+single-cell spatial profiling at a sensitivity comparable to
+Chromium.</p>
+<h2 id="cell-type-annotation-with-a-single-cell-reference">Cell-type
+Annotation with a Single-cell Reference</h2>
+<p>To annotate the matched ATERA and Xenium samples we used a previously
+published snRNA-seq breast cancer dataset (Janesick et al., 2023) as a
+reference. Annotation was performed with <a href="https://github.com/p-gueguen/rctd-py">rctd-py</a>, a fast Python
+reimplementation of <a href="https://github.com/dmcable/spacexr">RCTD</a>.</p>
+<blockquote>
+<p><strong>Note:</strong> SPLIT v0.2.0+ is annotation-tool agnostic –
+any deconvolution tool of your choice can be used (see the <a href="#split">SPLIT section</a> below).</p>
+</blockquote>
+<h3 id="reference-preparation">Reference preparation</h3>
+<p>The original reference contains mixed-cell-type clusters (“T Cell
+&amp; Tumor Hybrid”, “Stromal &amp; T Cell Hybrid”) that are removed
+prior to annotation. Cell types are also consolidated into three levels
+of granularity (Level 1-3).</p>
