+<p><strong>Summary:</strong> There is strong agreement between ATERA and
+Xenium annotations despite the former being derived from ~1,600 shared
+genes and the latter from 183, demonstrating that both technologies are
+compatible with label transfer. ATERA shows lower but detectable
+transcript spillover compared to Xenium. This reduced spillover is also
+evident in the UMAP embeddings below, where cell types in ATERA are
+better separated.</p>
